(&quot;No call times are open right now&quot;), get &quot;New times are open&quot; when the day is added.</div></aside></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'academy', 'chapter', 'hiring', null, 'Academy', 'Training paths by function: progress, opening a section early, editing lessons and questions, the gate.',
  'Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.

## Progress by staff member

1. Open **People** > **Academy**. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings > Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.
2. Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.
3. A section closed for them? Press **Open early**, give the reason and press **Open early** again. The reason is kept.

## Edit lessons and questions

1. Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.
2. **Edit the title** changes its name and what it covers.
3. Each lesson has **Preview** (the player) and **Edit the lesson**: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.
4. **Add a lesson**, **Delete** a lesson; each question has **Edit** (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and **Delete**; **Add a question** at the end.

## The pass mark and the gate

- Settings > Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).
- Academy gate (off by default): off, the academy only records progress. On, a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. Admins are never held.
- Take the Admin path yourself from **Take the Admin path**.',
  '<p class="gd-p">Training for every staff function: paths of sections, lessons played and narrated in the browser (no video files are stored), and a quiz per section.</p><section class="gd-task" id="academy-progress-by-staff-member" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Progress by staff member</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open <b class="gd-ui">People</b> &gt; <b class="gd-ui">Academy</b>. Each staff member shows their paths, sections passed and the last quiz. Settings &gt; Staff shows the same count in its Academy column.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open a person: each section with lessons watched, best score, attempts and its state.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">A section closed for them? Press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b>, give the reason and press <b class="gd-ui">Open early</b> again. The reason is kept.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-edit-lessons-and-questions" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Edit lessons and questions</h2><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Under Paths and sections, open a section. Changes apply at once for everyone.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Edit the title</b> changes its name and what it covers.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Each lesson has <b class="gd-ui">Preview</b> (the player) and <b class="gd-ui">Edit the lesson</b>: the title and the scenes. A scene is a caption, the words the voice says, and its picture: a title, a chat between the renter and you, a list, steps, money rows or a rule.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Add a lesson</b>, <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b> a lesson; each question has <b class="gd-ui">Edit</b> (the question, the options, the right answer counted from 0, and why) and <b class="gd-ui">Delete</b>; <b class="gd-ui">Add a question</b> at the end.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="academy-the-pass-mark-and-the-gate" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The pass mark and the gate</h2><ul class="gd-ul"><li>Settings &gt; Program: Academy: pass mark of a quiz (80% by default).</li><li>Academy gate (off by default): off, the academy only records progress. On, a staff member who has not passed every path of their functions opens only the academy, the guide and their profile. Admins are never held.</li><li>Take the Admin path yourself from <b class="gd-ui">Take the Admin path</b>.</li></ul></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'email-backups-and-site-health', 'chapter', 'maintenance-and-service', 'Keep an eye on email use against the daily limit, the nightly backup and the occasional error page.

## Email

**Settings** > **Email log**

1. The banner shows today''s emails against the daily limit. From 80, Admins get a notice; near the limit, digests and marketing wait first and booking and sign-in emails are held last.
2. Filter the Outbox: All, Queued, Held, Sent, Failed, Suppressed or Skipped.
3. Open an email to **Resend** or **Cancel** it.
4. Suppressions: **Suppress an address** stops all mail to it; **Lift** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-23-email-desktop-dad31712.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 760; address: carmacars.ca/admin/messages; pins: 1 56.5 31.7, 2 35.5 41.8, 3 81.9 52.6, 4 26.6 22.9")

## Backups

- The database is backed up every night, encrypted, kept for 30 days and test-restored on the spot.
- Every Monday the newest backup is checked again: it must be under 30 hours old and restore cleanly.
- A failed backup, or none for 30 hours, opens a site alert: an email (outside the quiet hours), a task and a line on To do. Tell your developer the same day.
- Keep a copy of the backup key in the company password manager. Without it no backup can be read.

## Site health and alerts

**Today** > **To do**, the Site health card at the bottom.

1. Every 5 minutes the site checks itself: the home page, a car page, the sign-in page and the site''s health check, and also emails, scheduled jobs, the nightly backup and Stripe payments.
2. Each line shows Working, Problem, Waiting for the website deploy or Not checked yet, what was found and how many checks failed in the last 24 hours.
3. Short problems, such as a single Error 1102, only show here and in your morning digest ("Site check: 6 failed checks in the last 24 hours, no alert email").
4. An email goes to rent@carmacars.ca only for a real outage: a page failing every check for 15 minutes, emails failing for 30 minutes, the nightly backup failing, or Stripe failing for 30 minutes. It also raises an urgent task and "Site problems found by the site check" first on To do. A failed scheduled job is never emailed.
5. At most 3 alert emails a day, and none from 11 pm to 7 am unless the whole site has been down for an hour. An outage held overnight is emailed at 7 am if it lasts. One "Recovered" email follows each alert, and the task closes by itself.
6. "Waiting for the website deploy" on the health check means the database was updated before the website: nothing is wrong, and it turns to Working after the deploy.

> Good to know: The alert address, the minutes before an email, the daily limit and the quiet hours are in Program settings, "Site check".

## When a page shows "Error 1102"

Our web host''s free plan sometimes stops a page that takes too long. Reload the page; you are still signed in. Moving to the Workers Paid plan removes it.
', 'Email, backups and site health', 'The email outbox and daily limit, suppressions, backups, the site check and its alerts, and Error 1102.',
  'Keep an eye on email use against the daily limit, the nightly backup and the occasional error page.

